"""Family A -- Brenz's bidding prayer (Schwäbisch Hall 1526) and its descendants.

Each petition is a bidding addressed to the people ("Lasset uns bitten für ...")
followed by a collect addressed to God.  Brenz's collects for the Church, for
the magistrates and for the afflicted are close renderings of the Good Friday
Orationes sollemnes (pro Ecclesia, pro imperatore, and bidding VI with its
collect "maestorum consolatio, laborantium fortitudo").
"""
from gp import P

# Luther's paraphrase of the Lord's Prayer (Deutsche Messe 1526), as used in
# Frankfurt 1553/1589 for the closing petition.
LP_PARA_EN = (
    "O Lord God, our Father in heaven, we thy wretched children upon earth beseech "
    "thee that thou wouldest look upon us mercifully and vouchsafe us grace, that thy "
    "holy name may be hallowed among us and in all the world, through the pure and "
    "right doctrine of thy word and through the fervent love of our life. Graciously "
    "turn away all false doctrine and evil life, wherein thy worthy name is blasphemed "
    "and put to shame. Thy kingdom come and be increased: bring all sinners, the "
    "blinded, and them that are taken captive of the devil into his kingdom, to the "
    "knowledge of the right faith in Jesus Christ thy Son, that the number of "
    "Christians may be great. Strengthen us, Lord, with thy Spirit, to do and to "
    "suffer thy will, both in life and in death, in good and in evil, that our will "
    "may at all times be broken, offered up, and slain. And give us our daily bread; "
    "keep us from covetousness and from the care of the belly, that we may look unto "
    "thee for all good things enough. Forgive us our debts, as we forgive our "
    "debtors, that our heart may have a sure and joyful conscience before thee, and "
    "may never fear nor be affrighted before any sin. Lead us not into temptation, "
    "but help us by thy Spirit to subdue the flesh, to despise the world with all "
    "its ways, and to overcome the devil with all his wiles. And at the last deliver "
    "us from all evil, both bodily and ghostly, temporal and eternal. Whosoever "
    "earnestly desire all this, let them say from the heart: Amen; believing without "
    "all doubt that it is Yea and heard in heaven, as Christ promiseth us: What "
    "things soever ye ask, believe that ye shall have them, and it shall be done. Amen.")

W = []

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
W.append(dict(
    key='schwaebisch_hall_1526', doc=754, year=1526,
    order='Schwäbisch Hall, Frühmessordnung (Johannes Brenz)',
    territory='Schwäbisch Hall (Imperial city)',
    citation='Sehling 17, I/1, pp. 37–40',
    family='A. Brenz bidding prayer', form='bidding + collect',
    tradition='Lutheran',
    position='After the Kyrie and Gloria, in place of the Latin Oremus/collect; read from a lectern before the altar in a cope. The sermon precedes the whole service.',
    heading='Gemein gebet fur die kirchen zu S[chwäbisch] Hal',
    heading_en='The common prayer for the Church at Schwäbisch Hall',
    notes='Base text A (StadtA Schwäbisch Hall 4/54); variants of MSS B and C in Sehling’s apparatus are not taken in. The Our Father, Creed and Decalogue are printed as part of the common prayer.',
    petitions=[
        P('exhortation',
          r='Vorrede', r_en='Preface',
          b='Auff das all glaubig zubeten gereitzt wurden, so hat unser Herr Cristus dem gebet ein ernstlich versicherung angehengkt, sprechendt: Bitten, so werden ir gewert, suchendt, so werden ir finden, klopffet an, so wirt euch auffgethon.',
          b_en='To the end that all the faithful might be stirred up to pray, our Lord Christ hath annexed unto prayer an earnest assurance, saying: Ask, and ye shall be granted; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you.'),
        P('church', sub='ministers',
          r='Für die kirchen und kirchendinern', r_en='For the Church and the ministers of the Church',
          b='Hieruff lassent uns fleyssig bitten fur die gemein cristenlich kirch, fur der kirchen diener, das sie unser Herr Got wolle beschutzen wider all anleuff und versuchung des boßen feinds, darmit sie auff dem starcken felsen, unserm Herrn Cristo, bestendig pleyben. Bittend Also:',
          b_en='Hereupon let us diligently pray for the common Christian Church, and for the ministers of the Church, that the Lord our God would defend them against all the assaults and temptation of the wicked enemy, that they may abide steadfast upon the strong rock, our Lord Christ. Pray ye thus:',
          p='Almechtiger, ewiger Got, der du hast allen volckern dein gnad durch Jesum Cristum geoffenbaret, erhalt, Herr, das volck deiner barmhertzikait, das dein kirch sampt irn dienern, in der gantzen welt zerstrewt, dir mit bestendigem glauben diene und in bekantnus deins namens bestande.',
          p_en='Almighty, everlasting God, who hast revealed thy grace unto all peoples through Jesus Christ: preserve, O Lord, the people of thy mercy, that thy Church together with her ministers, scattered abroad in the whole world, may serve thee with steadfast faith and continue in the confession of thy name.'),
        P('civil-authority',
          r='Fur die Oberkait', r_en='For the magistracy',
          b='Lassendt uns auch bitten auß gebot und bevelh unsers Herrn Jesu Cristi und seiner Apposteln fur unsern allergnedigsten Herrn, den kaiser, fur alle konig und amptlewt des weltlichen Regiments, sonderlich fur ein erbare Oberkait diser stat, auff das wir ein geruwigs und stils leben in aller gotselikait furen mogen. Bittend Allso:',
          b_en='Let us also pray, by the commandment and bidding of our Lord Jesus Christ and of his apostles, for our most gracious Lord the Emperor, for all kings and officers of the temporal government, and especially for an honourable magistracy of this city, that we may lead a quiet and peaceable life in all godliness. Pray ye thus:',
          p='Barmhertziger, ewiger Got, in welchs handt aller menschen gewalt und Oberkait besten, von dir verordnet zur straff der ubeltetter und wolfart der biderlewt, in welchs handt auch steen all Recht und gesatz aller Reich, Wir bitten dich, sihe gnedigklich auff unsern Herrn, den kaiser, und all sein amptlewt, nemlich auff ein Oberkait diser Stat, darmit sie das weltlich schwerdt, inen von dir bevolhen, in glauben nach deinem wort und bevelh furen mogen.',
          p_en='Merciful, everlasting God, in whose hand standeth the power and authority of all men, ordained of thee for the punishment of evildoers and for the welfare of the upright, in whose hand also stand all the rights and laws of all kingdoms: we beseech thee, look graciously upon our Lord the Emperor and all his officers, and namely upon the magistracy of this city, that they may bear the temporal sword, committed unto them of thee, in faith, according to thy word and commandment.'),
        P('afflicted', sub='error;calamities',
          r='Fur Irthumb und anfechtung', r_en='For error and temptation',
          b='Lassendt uns auch bitten Got, unsern Herrn, das er die welt von Irthum erlosen wol, auch von kranckhaiten, Tewerung, gefengknus, sterben und aller widerwertikait, so durch den bosen feindt uns zur verderpnus zugefugt werden. Bittend also:',
          b_en='Let us also pray God our Lord, that he would deliver the world from error, and also from sicknesses, dearth, imprisonment, death, and all adversity which by the wicked enemy is brought upon us unto our destruction. Pray ye thus:',
          p='Almechtiger, ewiger Got, ein trost der trawrigen, ein sterck der schwachen, laß fur dein angesicht durch unsern Herrn Jesum Cristum komen die bit aller deren, so in bekumernus unnd anfechtung zu dir seufftzen, das menigklich dein hilff und beystand in der zeyt der nodt entpfinde.',
          p_en='Almighty, everlasting God, the comfort of the sorrowful, the strength of the weak: let the prayer of all them that sigh unto thee in trouble and temptation come before thy face, through our Lord Jesus Christ, that every man may feel thy help and succour in the time of need.'),
        P('peace',
          r='Umb Friden', r_en='For peace',
          b='Lassendt uns auch bitten umb ein gemeinen friden und besserung der gantzen Cristenhait, das uns got mit zeitlichem und ewigklichem friden gnedigklich begabe. Bittend also:',
          b_en='Let us also pray for a common peace and for the amendment of all Christendom, that God would graciously endue us with temporal and everlasting peace. Pray ye thus:',
          p='Barmhertziger, ewiger Got, ein konig der himel und erden, durch welchs gaist alle ding regirt, durch welchs fursehung alle ding geordnet werden, ein Got des Frids, wir bitten dich durch unsern Herrn Jesum Cristum, du wollest unsern sunden vergeben und uns mit dem gaist des frids salben, darmit wir in forcht und zittern dir dienen, zu lob und preys deines namens.',
          p_en='Merciful, everlasting God, King of heaven and earth, by whose Spirit all things are governed, by whose providence all things are ordered, the God of peace: we beseech thee through our Lord Jesus Christ, that thou wouldest forgive our sins and anoint us with the spirit of peace, that we may serve thee in fear and trembling, to the laud and praise of thy name.'),
        P('enemies',
          r='Fur unsere Feind', r_en='For our enemies',
          b='Lassendt uns auch bitten fur unsere feind, das Got sie fur in ir aigne erkantnus und sie von irem unrechten abfur. Bittend also:',
          b_en='Let us also pray for our enemies, that God would lead them into the knowledge of themselves and lead them away from their unrighteousness. Pray ye thus:',
          p='Almechtiger, ewiger Got, der du uns durch deinen liben Son, unsern Herrn Jesum Cristum, bevolhen hast, das wir unsere feindt sollen liben, fur unsere verfolger bitten, wir schreyhen hertzlich zu dir, das du wellest unsere feind gnedigklich heimsuchen und inen ein fruntlich, einhellig gemut unnd hertz mit uns und der gantzen Cristenhait geben, durch unsern Herrn Jesum Cristum.',
          p_en='Almighty, everlasting God, who by thy dear Son, our Lord Jesus Christ, hast commanded us to love our enemies and to pray for our persecutors: we cry heartily unto thee, that thou wouldest graciously visit our enemies, and give them a friendly and one-accorded mind and heart with us and with all Christendom; through our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
        P('childbirth',
          r='Fur all schwanger Frawen', r_en='For all women with child',
          b='Lassendt uns bitten fur all schwanger frawen, das got sie gnedigklich von kinds banden erlosen wol. Bittend also:',
          b_en='Let us pray for all women with child, that God would graciously deliver them from the bonds of childbirth. Pray ye thus:',
          p='Barmhertziger, ewiger Got, der du man und weyp reichlich gesegnet hast, sprechend: Seyent fruchtbar und meret Euch, und dem weyp iren kumer im gebern zu einem hailigen Creutz durch unsern Herrn Jesum Cristum gemacht, wir bitten dich, Herr Got, du wollest die frucht irs leips, dein aigen werck, erhalten und sie underm Creutz der schmertzlichen geburt nit verderben laßen, sonder gnedigklich entpinden.',
          p_en='Merciful, everlasting God, who hast richly blessed man and woman, saying: Be fruitful and multiply; and hast made the woman’s sorrow in bearing an holy cross through our Lord Jesus Christ: we beseech thee, Lord God, that thou wouldest preserve the fruit of her womb, thine own work, and suffer her not to perish under the cross of the painful birth, but graciously deliver her.',
          note='Bid printed “erlosen wo”; the final l is lost in the OCR (cf. “erlosen wol” in the bid For error and temptation).'),
        P('fruits-of-earth',
          r='Fur die Fruchten der erden', r_en='For the fruits of the earth',
          b='Lassendt uns auch bitten fur die frucht der erden, das sie Got wol gesegnen und uns wol geraten lassen. Bittend also:',
          b_en='Let us also pray for the fruits of the earth, that God would bless them and let them prosper well for us. Pray ye thus:',
          p='Almechtiger, barmhertziger, ewiger Got, der du durch dein wort alle ding erschafest und gesegnest, wir bitten dich, das du den somen deins worts unsern Herrn Jesum Cristum, uns wollest mittailn und in unser Hertz sewen, dardurch an uns gesegnet werd mit fruchtbarer wachsung und gotlichem gebrauch alles, was uns zur leblichen noturft dienet.',
          p_en='Almighty, merciful, everlasting God, who through thy word createst and blessest all things: we beseech thee that thou wouldest impart unto us the seed of thy word, our Lord Jesus Christ, and sow him in our heart, whereby there may be blessed unto us, with fruitful increase and godly use, all that serveth us for our bodily need.'),
        P('lords-prayer', sub='conclusion',
          r='Gemein Gebet', r_en='Common prayer',
          b='Lassendt uns auch bitten sonst fur alles, so Got, unser Herr, gebetten sein wil, sprechend ein Vater unser.',
          b_en='Let us also pray besides for all things for which God our Lord will be prayed unto, saying an Our Father.'),
        P('lords-prayer',
          r='Des Herrn Gebet', r_en='The Lord’s Prayer',
          p='Vater unser in dem himel, etc.', p_en='Our Father, which art in heaven, etc.'),
        P('creed',
          r='Die bekantnus des Glaubens', r_en='The confession of the faith',
          p='Ich glaub in Got vater, almechtigen.', p_en='I believe in God the Father Almighty.'),
        P('decalogue',
          r='Die zehen gebot', r_en='The Ten Commandments',
          p='Disse wort hat der Herr alle geredt: Ich bin der Herr, etc.', p_en='The Lord spake all these words: I am the Lord, etc.'),
        P('special-supplications',
          r='Das wer nu fur das gemein gebet. Man mocht alwegen gebet hintzusetzen nach zufallenden sachen mit kriegen, pestilentz oder sonderlichen kranckhaiten, etc.',
          r_en='This, then, were for the common prayer. Prayers might always be added thereto according to matters as they befall, with wars, pestilence, or special sicknesses, etc.'),
    ]))

